Make the iso-codes package optional.

configure stops with "You must have iso-codes." when the package is not
installed, but the tables are only used to translate country and language
names (xkl_get_country_name, xkl_get_language_name), which read them at run
time and already cope with their absence (a warning, no name).  The layout
registry -- all liblightdm-gobject uses this library for -- does not touch
them.  Without the package configure now goes on and looks for the tables
under the install prefix.

